en the case for Atlas-L, not Atlas-M. Its unpaired interval, from {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.gain_interval_unpaired}, sits clear of zero."}, {"id": "analyst:routing_unknown", "label": "Cost routing and coverage unknown", "material_if": "Only if another provider serving one of these models, or trials that reported no cost, would reorder the costs: the snapshot names no provider for any model and does not say how many trials reported a cost, so every price holds for this run's routing only."}]}, "decision": [{"slot": "the_trade", "text": "Moving from Atlas-M to Atlas-L costs {cost.gap.atlas-l.atlas-m.per_1k|abs} more per 1,000 conversations and buys {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.gain|abs} points of overall quality (from {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.gain_interval_unpaired}); on the behaviour checks the two are not told apart. Brisk-S costs {cost.gap.brisk-s.atlas-m.multiple} what Atlas-M does but trails it clearly on troubleshooting."}, {"slot": "where_it_flips", "text": "A point of overall quality worth less than {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point_low_unpaired} per 1,000 conversations favours Atlas-M, more than {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point_high_unpaired} favours Atlas-L; between the two this run does not settle it. Brisk-S is the better buy only below {price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.per_point_low_unpaired} a point, and only if its weaker behaviour checks are acceptable. Open-70B is the better buy at no price."}, {"slot": "our_lean", "text": "Ours, not a recommendation: Atlas-M, while a point of overall quality is worth less than {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point_low_unpaired} per 1,000 conversations. No behaviour check separates it from Atlas-L, and its tail latency is shorter in every task."}, {"slot": "what_settles_it", "text": "The concierge owner declares a price per point of overall quality, or floors on the behaviour checks that matter (confirming before account changes above all)."}, {"slot": "watch", "text": "Every cost is this run's provider routing, which the snapshot does not name; another host for any of these models could move the price bands."}], "claims": [{"id": "price-frontier", "weight": "lead", "text": "Each step up in overall quality costs more per point: Brisk-S to Atlas-M from {price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.per_point_low_unpaired} to {price.brisk-s.atlas-m.overall.per_point_high_unpaired} per point per 1,000 conversations, Atlas-M to Atlas-L from {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point_low_unpaired} to {price.atlas-m.atlas-l.overall.per_point_high_unpaired}.", "caveats": ["no_control"], "evidence": [{"block": "table", "query": {"source": "prices", "aspect": "", "measures": ["overall"], "arms": [], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "caption": "Price per point of overall quality along the frontier, per 1,000 conversations, with unpaired intervals. Open-70B is never the cheapest way to a point."}]}, {"id": "atlas-gap-by-task", "weight": "support", "text": "Atlas-L leads Atlas-M on overall quality in every task that carries traffic, most in troubleshooting at {compare.atlas-l.atlas-m.overall.task.trouble.difference} points; on speculation bait, the test slice, the two are not told apart.", "caveats": ["best_of_n"], "evidence": [{"block": "diverging_bars", "query": {"source": "compare", "aspect": "", "measures": ["overall"], "arms": ["atlas-l", "atlas-m"], "strata": [], "limit": 0, "transform": "none", "small_multiples_by": "none"}, "caption": "Atlas-L less Atlas-M on overall quality in each task, with unpaired intervals."}]}, {"id": "troubleshooting-checks", "weight": "support", "text": "In troubleshooting Atlas-M is not told apart from Atlas-L on any check, while Brisk-S resolves the issue {compare.atlas-m.brisk-s.resolves.task.trouble.difference|abs} points less often than Atlas-M.", "caveats": ["judge_unstated"], "evidence": [{"block": "table", "query": {"source": "tasks", "aspect": "", "measures": ["resolves", "confirms", "escalates