rade; the appendix holds it."}, {"what": "Latency in the other tasks", "why": "Same order in every task as on research questions."}, {"what": "Overall quality per task for Brisk-S and Open-70B", "why": "Both sit below Atlas-M in most tasks; the pooled figures behind the price table carry the point."}, {"what": "A dominance call weighing quality beside cost", "why": "With no model-level quality figure, the computed dominance rested on cost alone and would name Brisk-S; the price frontier weighs cost against quality instead."}, {"what": "Failure examples", "why": "None were kept with this run."}], "next": [{"text": "The concierge owner declares a price per point of overall quality, or floors on the behaviour checks.", "settles": "Turns the trade into a decision between Atlas-M and Atlas-L, and says whether the cheaper models stay options."}, {"text": "Re-run Atlas-M and Atlas-L on the same cases with paired scoring.", "settles": "Whether the small behaviour-check gaps between them separate, and narrows the price band in which this run cannot choose."}, {"text": "Run a routed mix as a measured option: Atlas-M for most traffic, Open-70B for persona small talk.", "settles": "What the mix keeps of Atlas-M's quality and how much it saves, so it can be priced like the others; nobody has run it, so no figure states it yet."}, {"text": "Name the judge of the behaviour checks and calibrate it against human ratings.", "settles": "Whether the cheaper models' shortfalls on the checks are real or a judge's bias."}, {"text": "Record the provider serving each model, the cost coverage and the monthly volume of conversations.", "settles": "Whether the price bands hold beyond this run's routing, and what the trade is worth a month."}], "method": [{"term": "Cases", "text": "{scoreboard.atlas-l.cases} conversations per model over the tasks listed under traffic shares, the same count for each; repeats are not stated. No trial was lost or failed for any model."}, {"term": "Overall quality"